---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro';

const keyboardShortcuts = `// Keyboard Navigation & Action Shortcuts in Edit Mode
Cmd + S / Ctrl + S   -> Save pending edits to server (or Save Draft)
Escape               -> Deselect active text node / Close modal
Enter                -> In single-line mode: confirm & blur; in multiline: insert newline
Tab / Shift + Tab    -> Move caret focus to next / previous editable text node`;

const portalExample = `<!-- Dedicated isolated portal mount -->
<div id="copypatch-portal-root" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Edit Mode & Inline Mechanics"
  description="How ?copypatch=1 activation works, caret and selection persistence, Argon2id authentication, and floating toolbar controls."
>
  <h1>Edit Mode & Inline Mechanics</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    CopyPatch keeps the editor plane completely invisible and decoupled from public visitors until explicitly triggered by an authorized team member.
  </p>

  <h2>Activating Edit Mode</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Append <code>?copypatch=1</code> to your website URL (e.g. <code>https://my-app.com?copypatch=1</code>).</li>
    <li><code>CopyPatchProvider</code> detects the query parameter and dynamically lazy-loads the editor bundle (<code>~12 kB gzip</code>). Normal visitors never download this code.</li>
    <li>If no active session cookie exists, the <strong>Auth Modal</strong> prompts for the administrative passphrase.</li>
    <li>Upon authentication, the floating <strong>Toolbar</strong> mounts at the bottom of the viewport, and all <code>&lt;EditableText&gt;</code> elements display subtle editing affordances.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Native Caret & Selection Persistence</h2>
  <p>
    Unlike naive contenteditable wrappers that cause erratic cursor jumps when React re-renders, CopyPatch uses a custom caret preservation algorithm:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Nodes use native <code>contenteditable="plaintext-only"</code>, ensuring rich HTML formatting is stripped on paste.</li>
    <li>Edits are stored in an in-memory mutable store without triggering full component tree re-renders during keystrokes.</li>
    <li>When an element blurs or saves, React synchronizes state cleanly without disturbing text selection or active caret position.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Keyboard Shortcuts</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={keyboardShortcuts} lang="text" title="Keyboard Shortcuts" />

  <h2>Toolbar Controls Reference</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Control</th>
        <th>Visual Indicator</th>
        <th>Action</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Locale Indicator</strong></td>
        <td><code>EN</code> / <code>TR</code> pill</td>
        <td>Displays active editing language.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Status Badge</strong></td>
        <td>Green / Amber pulse dot</td>
        <td>Indicates whether changes are live (<code>Ready</code>) or pending (<code>Unsaved</code>).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Discard</strong></td>
        <td>Outlined button</td>
        <td>Reverts all pending inline changes back to the published snapshot.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Save (⌘S)</strong></td>
        <td>Primary blue pill</td>
        <td>Submits patch map to SQLite with optimistic revision verification.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Exit (✕)</strong></td>
        <td>Subtle icon button</td>
        <td>Removes <code>?copypatch=1</code> from URL and enters clean visitor mode.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>DOM Isolation & Portal Architecture</h2>
  <p>
    The toolbar and authentication modal render into a dedicated DOM container outside your application markup:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code={portalExample} lang="html" title="HTML" />

  <p>
    This guarantees that CopyPatch UI components never inherit application CSS resets, global form styles, or z-index layout clipping.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
